ders, against 2.9 and 4 for the 20k, and it never got back into the game.", "moments": [{"turn": 9, "text": "G6 had just followed White's F7, which handed Black a +1.4 lead. G6 lost 5.8 points and sent the lead to -4.4. The engine preferred F6. It was the first sizeable slip in an even opening."}, {"turn": 17, "text": "G5 stretched the Black group into a long line along row 5 (E5, F5, G5). It lost 8.1 points and dropped the lead from -2.9 to -11.0. The engine preferred D7. This is where the game stopped being close."}, {"turn": 19, "text": "H7 added another stone beside the G7 and G6 wall. It lost 10.1 points and took the lead from -11.6 to -21.7, a deficit Black never reduced much afterwards. The engine's choice was B5."}, {"turn": 22, "text": "White's D2 was the 20k's worst move, losing 11.7 points. It moved the lead from -21.3 to -9.7, and the 20k's stones on D1 and D2 pressed against Black's D3 group. For one move the game was open again."}, {"turn": 23, "text": "E3 gave back all of it. It lost 11.1 points and the lead fell from -9.7 to -20.7. The engine's choice was E2, the point White took next. After this the 20k held the bottom and left sides to the end."}, {"turn": 31, "text": "After White's H4 lost 10.5 points, Black found E7, the engine's own first choice, and lost only 0.1. The lead moved from -17.7 to -17.8. It was a tidy move, but the gap was too large for it to matter."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Every script only parsed the returned board (inspect: groups, liberties, empty regions), saved logs via apply_patch, converted the actual moves to SGF, replayed the historical moves to validate boards and captures, counted final area, and wrote notes to AGENTS.md. Nothing looped over empty points to score candidates or played continuations forward, and each move was passed by hand to mcp__go__play.", "stop": false}}